      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Generally, the incoming demographic driving renewal consists of younger, higher-earning professionals or affluent \"yuppies\" seeking urban living. Concurrently, the residents most at risk of displacement are often long-term, lower-income renters or minority populations with less housing security. This process creates a socioeconomic gap between the newcomers and the original community members. Ultimately, this displacement is a central, often negative, outcome of successful renewal projects.",
